      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=65957684\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium risk]** Changes when userbuffer communication overlap is enabled during forward pass\\.\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge; no blocking issue was identified in the changed forward-path selection.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nThe PR allows a requested LayerNormLinear forward UserBuffers all-gather overlap to run under `torch.no_grad()` while leaving backward-state checks unchanged.\n- The changed predicate makes the overlap path reachable during forward-only execution.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (3) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Merge branch &#39;main&#39; into codex/issue-290...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/249aa4ed55ca07b1b2588ed2501dd3b10375b429)</sub>",
